# Memo to the Rental Marketplace Dashboard Team

  During a review of the renter viewing data, I found that the dashboard is underreporting certain viewing outcomes.
  The report was intended to identify viewings that were not caused by a renter no-show,
  but it unintentionally excluded many viewings where no reason had been recorded.
  In our system, most attended and disputed viewings have a blank reason field because no cancellation occurred.
  These records should still be considered valid viewings, but they were omitted from the dashboard's calculation.

  The underlying data shows that there are three groups of viewings: those cancelled because of a renter no-show,
  those cancelled for another reason, and those where no cancellation reason exists because the viewing was completed or disputed.
   The dashboard only counted the second group and ignored the third group entirely.
   As a result, the number presented to users was lower than the true total. The issue does not come from bad data entered by renters or agents;
    it comes from the reporting logic treating blank values as if they did not exist.

  I recommend updating the dashboard so that viewings with no recorded cancellation reason are included
  whenever the goal is to count all viewings that were not renter no-shows. Once the logic is corrected,
  the report should be refreshed and any business decisions based on the previous numbers should be reviewed.
   This will ensure that property managers, agents, and analysts are working from a complete and accurate picture of renter activity.